            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0061" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111A Neutrality Patrol/68: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-18T13:00:00-06:00">January 18, 1940—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3. Department’s instruction No. 357, December 12, 1939. Memorandum just received
                    from the Foreign Office states that the Guatemalan Government will be pleased to
                    conclude arrangements envisaged in the above mentioned instruction. Will see the
                    Foreign Minister immediately to arrange exchange of memoranda in accordance with
                    the Department’s instruction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
